  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two vertical parallel mirrors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are separated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> cm. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> point object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The distance of the second nearest image behind mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;from the mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0097_d5f025a301f5.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 306px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0097_0770f7def78e.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 249px;\" /></p><p>As can be seen from the image above, object distance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> [For image by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>]</p><p>In a plane mirror the image distance is equal to the object distance. Thus, the required distance is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
